{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2670 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "247fedf61fcd8414e2a7b4211b6521c64759a0eb57ac469dca325595ca8b164a" :edb/db-before-t 2669 :edb/db-after-t 2670 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535982 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:14:56.691Z" 13194139535982 true] [17592186175863 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378130 13194139535982 true] [17592186175863 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378135 13194139535982 true] [17592186176021 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378141 13194139535982 true] [17592186176478 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535982 true] [17592186176478 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n$s(t) = t^{3} - 6t^{2}, t \\ge 0$.\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139535982 false] [17592186176478 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{3}-6{t}^{2},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139535982 true] [17592186176478 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-6{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-12t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-12t) \\\\  & =6t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6t-12 \\\\ 6t & =12 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=2.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\nv(2)=3(2)^{2}-12(2)=-12.\n$$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186293148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378129 13194139535982 true] [17592186378129 1034 "0" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378129 1111 #uuid "f34b1b58-ac4a-5dfa-a682-5a594e75d516" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378131 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378133 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1089 "q-335899" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1100 "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2),$ where $t>0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1113 #uuid "ba3fe1a8-417c-575a-af4e-f05aefe98151" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378130 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(\\sqrt{t}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\sqrt{t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-2}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}-\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}} & >0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & >0 \\\\ t & >{e}^{0} \\\\ t & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (1,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378132 13194139535982 true] [17592186378131 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378131 1041 "field-1" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378131 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378132 13194139535982 true] [17592186378131 1110 #uuid "0185a6b0-7069-562a-902a-0b5a963f1b2c" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378132 1034 "1" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378132 1111 #uuid "24e0216c-9d85-53ec-842c-438829e5f665" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378134 13194139535982 true] [17592186378133 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378133 1041 "field-2" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378133 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378134 13194139535982 true] [17592186378133 1110 #uuid "af780eb8-15d3-5e12-8877-f969496e14a6" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378134 1034 "\\infty" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378134 1111 #uuid "b7b74b36-88b4-5148-950f-f6c71fdb0c1b" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378136 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378139 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1089 "q-335904" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1100 "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by \n$s(t)=(4t-12)^{2},$\nwhere $t\\ge 0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in [${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1113 #uuid "91dc8f99-5321-572b-ae30-69b08a6cd471" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378135 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative.\n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,((4t-12)^{2}) \\\\  & =8(4t-12) \\\\  & =32(t-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x,$ we solve the inequality $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ 32(t-3) & <0 \\\\ t-3 & <0 \\\\ t & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$ is\n\n$$\nt\\in [0,\\,3).\n$$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378137 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378138 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1041 "field-1" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378138 13194139535982 true] [17592186378136 1110 #uuid "7d103569-a870-56b3-9514-c4f56a7b37eb" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378137 1034 "1" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378137 1111 #uuid "cc82e13f-8350-5567-8ed4-78673411281a" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378138 1034 "0" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378138 1111 #uuid "48cff5cf-d7bf-5985-8fb9-0c89c8061a62" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378139 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378140 13194139535982 true] [17592186378139 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378139 1041 "field-2" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378139 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378140 13194139535982 true] [17592186378139 1110 #uuid "1e5a32a8-9463-550c-9993-5dd9ca848442" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378140 1034 "3" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378140 1111 #uuid "8a705404-ea0c-560f-97d8-ab9760438fa4" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378142 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378144 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1089 "q-335917" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}ln\\,({t}^{2}),\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1113 #uuid "4e9f49e9-6a26-5990-8bb0-3a162ad2d69e" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378141 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\ns(t)={t}^{2}ln\\,({t}^{2})=2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(2t)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+2t) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+4t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a(t)=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+6 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) & =-6 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ t & ={e}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t={e}^{-3/2}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\,({e}^{-3/2}) & ={e}^{-3/2}(4ln\\,({e}^{-3/2})+2) \\\\  & ={e}^{-3/2}(4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})+2) \\\\  & ={e}^{-3/2}(-6+2) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t={e}^{-3/2},$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-4{e}^{-3/2}.$" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378143 13194139535982 true] [17592186378142 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378142 1041 "field-1" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378142 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378143 13194139535982 true] [17592186378142 1110 #uuid "39b5f636-31a1-540b-938c-5c6f76f457d6" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378143 1034 "e^{-3/2}" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378143 1111 #uuid "20008dbc-eda9-5408-87a2-e2c62f972573" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378145 13194139535982 true] [17592186378144 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535982 true] [17592186378144 1041 "field-2" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378144 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378145 13194139535982 true] [17592186378144 1110 #uuid "27220f10-dab9-5647-9caa-38641007c326" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378145 1034 "-4e^{-3/2}" 13194139535982 true] [17592186378145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535982 true] [17592186378145 1111 #uuid "38eb2b5a-f6d2-5dfd-9508-5a2ed16af9e7" 13194139535982 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-315550/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" 17592186378129 "q-335899" 17592186378130 "q-335899/field-1" 17592186378131 "q-335899/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186378132 "q-335899/field-2" 17592186378133 "q-335899/field-2/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" 17592186378134 "q-335904" 17592186378135 "q-335904/field-1" 17592186378136 "q-335904/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186378137 "q-335904/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" 17592186378138 "q-335904/field-2" 17592186378139 "q-335904/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955